t flour which  is a lot higher in fiber and protein and  those healthy fats than your traditional  wheat flour so I really love that for a  breading like this and then we add all  of our spices we've got some smoked  paprika a little bit of poultry  seasoning some brown sugar just a touch  you don't really need that much some  onion powder garlic powder some dried  parsley and good amount of pepper and  some salt so I'm going to shake this all  up get our shake and bake mix ready in  with our breasts so this recipe is also  really great for you know pork or any  other kind of poultry like Turkey would  also work really great as well seal up  the baggie and we already shake can we  dance this can we put some music on I  want y'all at home to get in with this  all right let's do  gonna get a good workout now's your  chance so here's a little quick tip I  always like to preheat my baking sheet  in a 400 degree oven so that way the  second the chicken goes down get a nice  golden crispy bottom as well as a nice  golden top because nobody likes a soggy  bottom right and the other thing I like  to do is just grab them these little oil  atomizers with some extra virgin olive  oil inside that way you can use a really  good high-quality olive oil and then  just give it a little spritz on top just  to get a little bit of extra browning  okay so these are gonna go into a 400  degree oven for about 25 to 30 minutes  usually get nice and golden brown and  they reach an internal temperature of  about 165 Fahrenheit  so good mom you're never going to need  that box version again I think this is  gonna make the best last recipe in my  little pretty printed cookbook I cannot  wait to see my parents reactions to this  so guys if you liked what you saw be  sure to check out the other two videos  with recipes that are featured in this  little cookbook give me the thumbs up  big ones please leave me a comment below  with some of your family's favorite  recipes subscribe to the channel a